# Line endings.
#
# This package is developed inside a monorepo on Windows, where core.autocrlf
# turns the working tree into CRLF. `dart pub publish` packs the WORKING TREE,
# not the git blob, so a shell script checked out here reaches every consumer
# with CRLF. Measured 2026-08-03 by unpacking the published rk_syslog 0.2.1:
# all 79 lines of apple/build_rust.sh were CRLF, line 32 being `set -eu`.
#
# What then happens on a consumer's Mac: /bin/sh reads `set -eu` as a command
# whose name ends in a carriage return, prints
#
#   apple/build_rust.sh: line 32: : command not found
#   apple/build_rust.sh: line 33: set: -: invalid option
#
# and carries on. `set -eu` never took effect, the `: "${VAR:?}"` guards never
# ran, cargo was never invoked -- and the script EXITS 0 having built nothing.
# A green build that ships no library is the worst outcome available, and this
# repository had already met it once on Android.
#
# This file must live in the package, not only in the monorepo root: the public
# mirror takes this directory as its repository root and would not inherit it.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.podspec text eol=lf
